# Node / Playwright
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright/.cache/

# Generated test reports (regenerated locally; never committed)
coverage/
playwright-report/

# UI audit output (regenerated on every `ui-audit.mjs` / `flow-walk.mjs`
# run; ~25MB of PNGs). The Playwright BASELINES under
# tests-mockups/baselines/ ARE committed — they are regression gates.
# These are not: they are a record of one audit pass.
ui-audit-shots/

# Local curl cookie jars used by the manual smoke-test loop.
# These carry live `cityfix_session` cookies — never commit them.
cf-cookies.txt

# Generated Playwright test outputs (baselines live in tests-mockups/baselines/ and ARE committed)
tests-mockups/artifacts/
tests-mockups/artifacts/**
tests-mockups/html-report/
# Diff images copied out of the container by the two-baseline diagnostic
# (scripts/run-two-baseline-diag.sh) — a debugging aid, not a deliverable.
tests-mockups/diffs/

# Per-run UI audit captures. Each spec (02-live-audit, 03-authenticated-flow,
# 04-e2e-human-tester, …) writes its screenshots here on every run, so the
# tree churns on each suite execution. These are a record of ONE audit pass,
# not regression gates — the gates are the `toHaveScreenshot` baselines under
# tests-mockups/baselines/. The spec headers say as much ("Screenshots from
# this spec are NOT committed baselines and are gitignored"); this rule is
# what makes that true.
tests-mockups/audit/

# Local visual-check renders from `node scripts/render-mockups.mjs`. These
# are a developer's eyeball pass on Windows; the committed baselines under
# tests-mockups/baselines/ are produced by CI on ubuntu-latest and are the
# only regression gate.
tests-mockups/scratch-render/

# Ad-hoc screenshot captures written by the throwaway Playwright probes
# used while debugging a surface (e.g. tests/tmp/pg-shots/**). These are
# a record of ONE debugging pass, not regression gates.
#
# Deliberately a PATH rule, not a `*.png` rule. Two image trees ARE
# tracked and must stay that way:
#   - tests-mockups/baselines/**  — the Playwright `toHaveScreenshot`
#     regression gates, regenerated on CI (ubuntu-latest).
#   - tests/fixtures/after-photo.png — a real fixture the crew
#     after-photo upload spec reads off disk.
# A blanket extension ignore would silently untrack both and quietly
# break the upload spec and the visual gates.
tests/tmp/

# Loose screenshot drops anywhere in the tree (the probes above wrote
# into the repo root during development). Catches a stray capture that
# lands outside tests/tmp/, without touching the tracked trees above.
# An already-tracked PNG is unaffected by this rule — git only ignores
# untracked files — and the negations keep NEW baseline/fixture PNGs
# addable.
#
# Note: no rule for .mockup-backup/ — it is already excluded as a
# directory, and git never descends into an excluded directory, so a
# negation for it would be dead weight.
*.png
!tests-mockups/baselines/**/*.png
!tests/fixtures/*.png
!design-artifacts/**/*.png
!public/**/*.png

# Next.js build output
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts.bak
# TypeScript incremental build cache (regenerated by tsc --noEmit / next build)
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment files (kept out of the repo for civic-platform security posture)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# Next.js auto-generated TypeScript shim (regenerated on every build)
next-env.d.ts

# Per-developer MCP server config (consumes env-var secrets; not for the shared repo)
.mcp.json

# Per-developer AI agent tooling installations (not project code)
# Per AGENTS.md, the WDS standalone install lives outside the repo. These
# trees are local CLI/framework state and would be reinstalled per-developer
# via their respective installers.
#
# .claude/ holds the specsmd installer-generated slash commands and agent
# definitions (`.claude/commands/specsmd-*.md`, `.claude/agents/specsmd-*.md`).
# `npx specsmd@latest install` writes them into relative `.claude/commands`
# and `.claude/agents` paths, so the registration lands here and nowhere
# else. It is per-developer state like the rest of this block: the durable
# record is the committed memory bank under
# .specsmd/aidlc/memory-bank/, and the registration is recreated by
# re-running the installer. Ignoring it keeps a `git add .` or `git clean`
# from sweeping away the developer's command registration.
#
# This rule was added 2026-11-14 after the AIDLC-lane removal (7e9b073)
# took the old runner's tree with it and left specsmd's own `.claude/`
# registration absent — the commands were simply not registered for
# anyone, with nothing in version control to restore them from.
.claude/
#
# Note on .specsmd/: the canonical specsmd memory bank
# (.specsmd/aidlc/memory-bank/**) IS
# committed to main as the team's durable brief artefact (intent
# briefs, unit briefs, bolt records, story index, decision log,
# standards). Only the per-developer runtime cache (agents, scripts,
# skills, templates) stays gitignored, as a re-pull of the specsmd
# framework replaces those locally without touching the briefs.
#
# The paths in .specsmd/aidlc/memory-bank.yaml resolve relative to
# .specsmd/aidlc/, so `.specsmd/aidlc/memory-bank/` is the only
# memory-bank path. A stray `.specsmd/memory-bank/` once held one
# duplicate of a story file; it was removed 2026-11-10.

# specsmd runtime cache (per-developer; re-installed by the specsmd
# framework). The memory bank (intents/bolts/standards/story-index.md
# /project.yaml/maintenance-log.md) is the team's durable record and
# is the default-untracked state under .specsmd/. We do NOT use a
# broad `.specsmd/` ignore here because that pattern blocks `git add`
# from materializing the memory bank (git's add path is more
# conservative than check-ignore). Instead, the runtime-cache
# subtrees below are explicitly excluded, and the framework's own
# distributable files (README, manifest, quick-start, context-config,
# memory-bank.yaml) are excluded by name. Everything else under
# .specsmd/ is implicitly committed.
.specsmd/aidlc/agents/
.specsmd/aidlc/scripts/
.specsmd/aidlc/skills/
.specsmd/aidlc/templates/
.specsmd/aidlc/README.md
.specsmd/aidlc/manifest.yaml
.specsmd/aidlc/context-config.yaml
.specsmd/aidlc/memory-bank.yaml
.specsmd/aidlc/quick-start.md

